# One immutable-old nonfinal Return frontier acceptance unit

Design only, 2026-10-18. No tests, builds, formatting, SQL execution, containers, repository edits, or external writes were performed for this plan. Repository inspected: `/Users/marcelo/Documents/Projects/sagat-octopus-project-completion`, current production pin `f81a1285a4d26bb1897ef4f178bafbbb65c5ad5d`; immutable old production pin `6c44a0e49670cf19660792cd1518d241e6c99b3b`.

## Selected outcome and boundary

Accept only §11.4 frontier case **(b), a pending NONFINAL Return**: genuine old closed root collection owners make E exceed 4 MiB although the stored ledger L fits. Old c10 has one genuinely completed compensable work activity, its pending Return, and an unadmitted second item. One current normal `Scheduler::advance_collection` must return `DrainStarted` with `ExistingOutputs` evidence before checkpointing that Return or admitting item 1. Continue the resulting obligation through ordinary current compensation and finalization.

This is an acceptance increment over the already present guard, with no anticipated production change. Free-admission, live-only Waiting, E==limit, competing stops, held-lock/CAS races, in-flight reports, Applied, uncertain COMMIT, rollout, and general nested capacity are separate work. In particular, the existing ce6560c5 live-worker case is not the selected pending-Return case. Q7c/Q8/Q9, master Q, and canonical 014 checkboxes remain open after this narrow evidence. Trace to FR-014-004/005/014, NFR-014-001/003, SC-014-005 and correction §11.3–11.4; no new product decision or capability is needed.

## Source grounds

- Current registered module is `tests/integration/workflow-primitives/legacy_collection_output_view.rs` (`main.rs:47`). Its companion runner is `scripts/test-legacy-collection-output-view.sh`; the actual overlay is `tests/fixtures/legacy-collection-output/producer.rs`. No new module registration is needed.
- Existing overlay `document`, `finish_then_hold`, `assert_shape` currently makes **one-item** scopes and requires one later LEASED work step. The consumer `legacy_scheduler_case` (`:773`) checks a live c10 lease, starts discovery with `tick`, then waits for expiry. Neither helper is the new handoff contract. Keep the existing Q5 matrix path intact and add a separate producer/test/receipt variant in these same files.
- Old `crates/infra-ir/src/convert.rs:701–792` permits root collection chains ending at End and multiple referenced bodies, each an activity chain ending at Return. The new two-body graph is within that old public shape.
- Old `crates/application/src/worker/scoped_reports.rs:180–317` retains successful forward output and calls `complete_path_instance`; old `crates/domain/src/execution/command.rs:580` applies success and settles routing. Old `execution/plan.rs:166–237` routes the completed activity, creates its successor, and deliberately leaves a Return PENDING. Therefore **no old scheduler tick is needed or allowed after c10's first successful CompleteStep**.
- Old `crates/infra-postgres/src/primitives.rs:1419` checkpoints actual Return payloads; `:2550` stores collection result/finish and routes the owner without the current owner-output logical charge. Current `collection_outputs.rs:285–300` adds each missing legacy owner output length separately, even for equal digests.
- Current `crates/infra-postgres/src/scope_frontier.rs:45–105,251–384` takes a repeatable-read snapshot, reads E with the run revision/stop metadata, and hydrates only active member data. `application/scope_frontier.rs:62–78` recognizes an actual PENDING Return.
- Current `crates/scheduler/src/passes.rs:647` is the normal public entry; `:1816–1837` first uses the frontier. Within OPEN, `:1940` selects ExistingOutputs before the pending Return loop; `:2000` distinguishes a last Return via `completed + 1 == item_count` and otherwise calls the checkpoint path.
- Current `crates/infra-postgres/src/primitives.rs:888` independently requires E>limit with no existing stop for ExistingOutputs. `start_collection_drain` (`:2406`) checks native authority/revision, writes the first stop and truthful drain, audit, outbox and telemetry atomically. With no live attempt the first call has exactly two new events; pending Return cancellation belongs to later member drain.
- Current `scheduler/passes.rs:1699–1810` resumes draining before full data hydration and plans compensation. `primitives.rs:3021` requires that saga to finish before finalization. Existing `byte_ceilings.rs:719–777` demonstrates the expected FAILED scope / COMPENSATED run / DONE-COMPENSATED saga combination.
- **Version-specific role warning:** the inspected **immutable-old 6c44a0e4** `tests/support/scope_flow.rs::Flow::start` explicitly passes `Options { runtime_role: true, .. }`. Do not use that constructor to claim the new owner-mode producer. Use old `tests/support/worker.rs::platform_with` with an explicitly selected `Options.runtime_role`, plus its ordinary public worker protocol and a normal fenced scheduler. Use the existing membership bootstrap followed by the public exact worker-binding endpoint (as old Flow does); do not call `Platform::worker`/`bind_everything`, which inserts binding rows with fixture SQL. This observation makes no claim about current Flow or the actual roles of earlier evidence. The new phases must print/assert their own actual roles.
- Current pinned `tests/support/mod.rs::attach_existing_db`, `tests/support/api.rs::start_on_db`, and `tests/support/worker.rs::Platform::connect` / `Worker::register_version` already support the current compensation process. They need no change and no unfinished P0b work. A fresh current worker session is legitimate: this fixture has no remaining old forward report to submit.

